.Nd relocation construction, inspection, and backend dispatch for libelfobj
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In elfobj.h
.Ft elf_err_t
.Fn elf_add_relocation "elf_section_t *section" "uint64_t offset" "elf_symbol_t *symbol" "uint32_t type" "int64_t addend"
.Ft size_t
.Fn elf_section_reloc_count "const elf_section_t *section"
.Ft elf_reloc_t *
.Fn elf_section_reloc_at "elf_section_t *section" "size_t index"
.Ft elf_reloc_t *
.Fn elf_reloc_at "elfobj_t *obj" "size_t index"
.Ft uint64_t
.Fn elf_reloc_offset "const elf_reloc_t *reloc"
.Ft uint32_t
.Fn elf_reloc_type "const elf_reloc_t *reloc"
.Ft int64_t
.Fn elf_reloc_addend "const elf_reloc_t *reloc"
.Ft int
.Fn elf_reloc_has_addend "const elf_reloc_t *reloc"
.Ft elf_symbol_t *
.Fn elf_reloc_symbol "const elf_reloc_t *reloc"
.Ft elf_section_t *
.Fn elf_reloc_section "const elf_reloc_t *reloc"
.Ft elf_err_t
.Fn elf_set_reloc_hooks "elfobj_t *obj" "const elf_reloc_hooks_t *hooks" "void *user"
.Ft elf_err_t
.Fn elf_apply_relocation "const elf_reloc_t *reloc" "uint64_t place" "uint64_t sym_value" "uint64_t *out_value"
.Ft elf_err_t
.Fn elf_apply_relocation_value "const elfobj_t *obj" "uint32_t type" "uint64_t place" "uint64_t sym_value" "int64_t addend" "uint64_t *out_value"
.Ft int
.Fn elf_reloc_size_for_machine "uint16_t machine" "uint32_t type"
.Ft int
.Fn elf_reloc_is_pc_relative_for_machine "uint16_t machine" "uint32_t type"
.Ft int
.Fn elf_reloc_is_tls_for_machine "uint16_t machine" "uint32_t type"
.Ft elf_err_t
.Fn elf_register_reloc_backend "const struct elf_reloc_backend *backend"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Relocations can be added to sections, enumerated at section/object scope,
and evaluated through the registered backend for a target machine.
.Pp
.Fn elf_apply_relocation
evaluates the exact relocation record.
.Fn elf_apply_relocation_value
evaluates from explicit relocation parameters without an
.Vt elf_reloc_t
handle.
.Pp
Hook callbacks installed via
.Fn elf_set_reloc_hooks
are invoked before/after relocation application and for incremental notes.
These hooks are intended for linker instrumentation and diagnostics.
.Pp
Backend helpers report relocation width and semantics for machine/type pairs:
.Bl -tag -width elf_reloc_is_pc_relative_for_machine
.It Fn elf_reloc_size_for_machine
Returns relocated field width in bytes, or -1 if unknown.
.It Fn elf_reloc_is_pc_relative_for_machine
Returns non-zero for PC-relative relocation classes.
.It Fn elf_reloc_is_tls_for_machine
Returns non-zero for TLS relocation classes.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn elf_section_reloc_count
returns the number of relocation entries for a section.
.Pp
.Fn elf_section_reloc_at
and
.Fn elf_reloc_at
return NULL when
.Fa index
is out of range.
.Pp
Other APIs return
.Dv ELF_OK
on success and an
.Vt elf_err_t
on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
